course: dictionary
lesson: 4902
title: Illusions: when your eyes are fooled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An illusion is something that seems real or true but is not. Your eyes and brain can be tricked, so what you see is not always what is there. «The stage magician made the box look empty, but it was an illusion.» Nothing vanished; the magician used special boxes, mirrors and hidden helpers.
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so use the clues around it. In «The two lines looked different lengths, but a ruler showed they were the same», the words ruler and showed tell you that illusion means a trick of the eyes. Check by swapping in another word, such as trick, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Illusion can also mean a false belief. «He was under the illusion that school was cancelled» means he wrongly thought it was cancelled. The clue is under: he believed something that was not true. Ask yourself: was it really true?
fact: Illusion means something that seems real or true but is not.
fact: An optical illusion is a picture or pattern that tricks your eyes.
fact: «The Müller-Lyer illusion» makes two equal lines look different lengths, because of their arrow ends.
fact: «A mirage in the desert» is a real illusion of water; the water is not really there.
fact: Your brain guesses what you see, and it can be fooled.
exercise: «The magician's trick made the box look empty, but it was an illusion.» What is an illusion here? | *Something that seems real or true but is not | A kind of stage light | A wooden tool for cutting | A large animal
exercise: «He was under the illusion that school was cancelled.» What does illusion mean here? | *A false belief | A kind of weather | A stage show | A ruler
exercise: Why do two equal lines with arrow ends look different lengths? | Because the ruler is bent | *Because of the arrow ends, which trick the brain | Because one is painted red | Because one line is longer
test: «A stick in water looks bent, but the look is an illusion.» What does the word illusion tell us? | It means the water is deep | *It looks true but is not | It is always a lie told on purpose | It is a kind of stick
test: Which one is an optical illusion? | *A picture that makes two equal lines look different lengths | A ruler that measures exactly 30 centimetres | A sunset with orange clouds | A glass of clear water
exam: Omar says the moon looks huge near the horizon, so it must be bigger there. Is he right? | Yes, because the moon is closer to Earth at the horizon | *No, it is about the same size all night, so this is an illusion | Yes, because the sky is smaller there | Yes, the moon grows bigger each hour
